[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3635507392","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3635507392","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3635507392,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YsXDA","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T05:52:17Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T05:52:17Z","body":"`Resource` inherit `RefCounted`. When a `RefCounted` object has no remaining references, it is deleted from memory. This is a common mistake when creating or loading a resource into a local variable. Local variables are deleted when the function/block ends.\n\nYou should either add `await` before calling the async method `getData()` or assign the resource instance to a member variable instead of a local variable.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3635507392/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637321432","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3637321432","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3637321432,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YzR7Y","user":{"login":"wyu100","id":98268563,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdt1kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98268563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100","html_url":"https://github.com/wyu100","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T14:21:48Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T14:22:53Z","body":"That makes sense! I wasn't exactly sure whether or not this was the intended outcome. I would recommend adding a warning so that the problem isn't completely invisible if someone writes this code, so that it is easier to debug.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637321432/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637342032","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3637342032","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3637342032,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YzW9Q","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T14:25:58Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T14:25:58Z","body":"There really wouldn't be a good way to determine if a warning is needed, if it isn't a temporary then it's perfectly valid code","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637342032/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637406859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3637406859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3637406859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YzmyL","user":{"login":"wyu100","id":98268563,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdt1kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98268563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100","html_url":"https://github.com/wyu100","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T14:40:29Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T14:40:29Z","body":"I'm not super familiar with how Godot detects warnings in code. Is there a way to check if a variable is local to a function?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637406859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637495561","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3637495561","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3637495561,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Yz8cJ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T14:57:19Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T14:57:19Z","body":"It's more complicated in this case, for example this code would work fine:\n```gdscript\nvar resource_instance=preload(\"res://test_resource.gd\").new()\n\t\nresource_instance.getData()\n\nawait get_tree().create_timer(2.0).timeout\n```\nSo it would be generally impossible to analyze this from just the code, how would, for example, this behave:\n```gdscript\nvar resource_instance=preload(\"res://test_resource.gd\").new()\n\t\nresource_instance.getData()\n\nawait some_class.some_signal\n```\n\nSo the only thing that would be possible here would be a warning if an `await` is finished after a class is freed, and there is such a check, I'm not sure under what conditions that fires and why it doesn't in this case, the check is here:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d743736f84fb668bcdfb5bf86258e483f35c6fec/modules/gdscript/gdscript_function.cpp#L202-L208","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637495561/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637520520","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3637520520","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3637520520,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y0CiI","user":{"login":"wyu100","id":98268563,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdt1kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98268563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100","html_url":"https://github.com/wyu100","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T15:02:45Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T15:02:45Z","body":"Is it possible that the `Resource` doesn't get added to the `instances_list`?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637520520/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637562445","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3637562445","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3637562445,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y0MxN","user":{"login":"wyu100","id":98268563,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdt1kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98268563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100","html_url":"https://github.com/wyu100","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T15:11:33Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T15:34:02Z","body":"I just looked through the code and I was wondering if this is part of the issue in `gdscript_vm.cpp`:\nit appears that they are only added if they are signals\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d743736f84fb668bcdfb5bf86258e483f35c6fec/modules/gdscript/gdscript_vm.cpp#L2593C5-L2593C21\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d743736f84fb668bcdfb5bf86258e483f35c6fec/modules/gdscript/gdscript_vm.cpp#L2610-L2615","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637562445/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637763433","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3637763433","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3637763433,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y091p","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T15:53:44Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T16:00:05Z","body":"I don't think we can add any new warnings for this case, either at compile time or, especially, at runtime (you can't ignore errors/warnings at runtime). This case is indistinguishable from valid use cases.\n\nPreviously, Godot printed errors when an object with uncompleted coroutines was destroyed, but this caused user frustration due to false positives. Essentially, you either couldn't reliably use `await` unless you were sure the expected signal would be emitted before the object was destroyed, or you had to live with the occasional false positive errors in the log.\n\n* If you think that missing `await` is the error you made in this case, you can try enabling the new warning `MISSING_AWAIT` (introduced in 4.6).\n* If you think the cause of the error is improper memory management, such static analysis is very complex and is completely absent from the current GDScript implementation. I don't think we should expect it to appear in the near future.\n* If you think the error is caused by deleting an object with uncompleted coroutines, we could potentially add a runtime warning (the old unpopular behavior), but keep in mind that the option to enable/disable it would be global, not case-by-case. You wouldn't be able to suppress it only in a specific location (we don't have a system for marking and filtering runtime errors/warnings based on their source location).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637763433/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637886528","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3637886528","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3637886528,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y1b5A","user":{"login":"wyu100","id":98268563,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdt1kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98268563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100","html_url":"https://github.com/wyu100","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T16:18:35Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T16:18:35Z","body":"I think that 3rd option is the real issue that is happening. It can sometimes be hard to debug if you don't realize what's happening. I do see how it would be unpopular because it could create a lot of unnecessary warnings for code that is intentionally destroying classes before coroutines complete. I don't know how practice it would be but if you could detect that an object was deleted with an incomplete coroutine because it was stored in a local function variable when the function ended. That would fix this issue while not creating a whole lot of unnecessary warnings.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637886528/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638033970","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3638033970","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3638033970,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y1_4y","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T16:49:49Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T16:49:49Z","body":"> I don't know how practice it would be but if you could detect that an object was deleted with an incomplete coroutine because it was stored in a local function variable when the function ended\n\nThis is called \"exception-based programming\". The problem is that if we can't find a coherent logical model, just adding more individual cases isn't a good idea in the long run. It's an attempt to patch over more fundamental design limitations, which have their pros and cons.\n\nIt could be that the object with the uncompleted coroutine wasn't stored in a local variable, but in an array inside a local variable. It could be that the object was created in a local variable but then assigned to a member variable, or that this object registers itself (inside the constructor) in some global object upon creation, so the warning would still be a false positive.\n\nI'd say the problem lies in the discrepancy between user intuitive expectations and understanding of how things actually work. If you use `await`, you should understand that the function may never complete, either because the awaited signal/coroutine doesn't complete or because the instance is destroyed before the awaited event occurs. If you create objects, you should consider their lifetime, and so on.\n\nUnderstanding many non-obvious things is an inevitable part of the learning process. The only thing we can do is improve the documentation to make this process easier for users and try to prevent some misconceptions that may arise.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638033970/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638114231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113832#issuecomment-3638114231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113832","id":3638114231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y2Te3","user":{"login":"wyu100","id":98268563,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdt1kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98268563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100","html_url":"https://github.com/wyu100","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wyu100/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T17:10:04Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T17:10:04Z","body":"I completely agree that adding specific cases to resolve edge cases is a terrible solution! I also think that I probably should have realized that it was possible for my resource to be deleted, but I wasn't paying attention to the fact that it was being stored in a local variable. If it was in the docs under `Resource` or `Await` it might be noticeable enough that people would be informed.\n\nJust another thought that may or may not be helpful. If there was an option like `debug > show object cleanup` that essentially showed when things got deleted in the console it could also reveal this issue.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3638114231/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]